1
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:41,719
Commissar Pei.

2
00:01:43,959 --> 00:01:44,359
Old Tan.

3
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:46,359
We're here to learn from Headquarters.

4
00:01:46,359 --> 00:01:46,760
Not at all.

5
00:01:46,799 --> 00:01:47,760
We're learning from each other.

6
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:48,439
This way.

7
00:01:48,439 --> 00:01:48,799
Welcome, welcome.

8
00:01:49,159 --> 00:01:51,519
This is Commander Liao from our Special Police Unit.

9
00:01:51,519 --> 00:01:51,959
Welcome, welcome.

10
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:52,640
Thanks for coming all this way.

11
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,079
Captain Liu.

12
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,840
Commissar Pei. Long time no see.

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:55,319
Welcome.

14
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:56,480
How about this?

15
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,519
Let's go to the lounge.

16
00:01:57,519 --> 00:01:58,719
Take a break and have some water.

17
00:01:59,159 --> 00:01:59,680
We'll follow your lead.

18
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,519
No need for that just yet.

19
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,680
Let's just start the tour.

20
00:02:02,359 --> 00:02:03,719
All right, let's start the tour then.

21
00:02:04,159 --> 00:02:05,000
Tell you what, you ride in my car.

22
00:02:05,079 --> 00:02:05,280
Let's go.

23
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:06,040
Alright, alright.

24
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:06,560
See you in a bit.

25
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,360
Come this way, Comrades.

26
00:02:36,159 --> 00:02:36,759
Let's head inside.

27
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:37,719
This is the indoor shooting range.

28
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,080
This shooting range of ours

29
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:42,000
can be adapted based on different training plans

30
00:02:42,599 --> 00:02:45,719
to simulate various terrains and climates at any time.

31
00:02:46,159 --> 00:02:48,479
This greatly enhances our Special Police Unit members'

32
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:49,599
adaptability.

33
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:51,120
Step this way.

34
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,159
Come, you can see everything from here.

35
00:02:53,439 --> 00:02:54,159
Step further inside, come on.

36
00:02:54,439 --> 00:02:56,840
The screen up there is connected to the inside.

37
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:59,280
You can see the exact scores hit on the targets inside.

38
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:02,080
Come, everyone take a look. How is it?

39
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,719
As for training,

40
00:03:04,759 --> 00:03:05,240
Headquarters has always...

41
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,400
Now this is a smart shooting range!

42
00:03:06,919 --> 00:03:07,919
...been the leader of the whole province.

43
00:03:07,919 --> 00:03:08,960
It's quite different from ours.

44
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:10,520
We don't dare slack off for a single moment.

45
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,919
The leaders gave the word.

46
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,400
We must be the best in the province,

47
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,800
and among the top in the country.

48
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,400
The facilities are fantastic.

49
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:23,199
This standard is definitely up to international levels.

50
00:03:24,199 --> 00:03:25,000
There's no need to be jealous.

51
00:03:25,319 --> 00:03:26,599
There are plenty of ping-pong tables,

52
00:03:26,639 --> 00:03:28,039
but isn't there only one Ma Long?

53
00:03:28,319 --> 00:03:28,840
The key is,

54
00:03:29,199 --> 00:03:31,280
it still depends on the members' quality and training.

55
00:03:31,319 --> 00:03:32,039
Right, right, right.

56
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,879
That's why we're here to learn from Headquarters.

57
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,560
Commissar Pei, you have to help us out.

58
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,639
Pass on some of your experience.

59
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,520
Absolutely.

60
00:03:39,919 --> 00:03:42,639
It just so happens there's outdoor training today.

61
00:03:42,759 --> 00:03:43,639
Everyone is here.

62
00:03:44,319 --> 00:03:44,919
That's perfect timing.

63
00:03:45,319 --> 00:03:47,280
Let's hurry outside to learn a thing or two.

64
00:03:47,599 --> 00:03:48,000
Commissar Pei,

65
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,439
can I take my men to fire a few rounds?

66
00:03:50,719 --> 00:03:52,120
You can fire ten rounds, no problem.

67
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,039
That's great!

68
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:55,319
Tulong, go arrange the target practice.

69
00:03:57,639 --> 00:03:59,560
Do you know why I chose to come today?

70
00:04:00,159 --> 00:04:01,719
I asked around in advance.

71
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,759
They're doing full-team training today.

72
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,319
We need to seize the opportunity

73
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:06,759
to observe our opponents.

74
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,000
The main thing is to observe our opponents.

75
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:10,280
Got it.

76
00:04:11,199 --> 00:04:13,680
Commissar Pei, let's go check out the training ground first.

77
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,120
You can shoot in a bit.

78
00:04:15,479 --> 00:04:15,960
Sure.

79
00:04:16,519 --> 00:04:18,199
So, whatever requests you have today,

80
00:04:18,319 --> 00:04:18,959
just ask.

81
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,519
You can train however you want.

82
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,560
Thanks. Thank you.

83
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,399
It's no big deal at all.

84
00:04:23,399 --> 00:04:23,800
Let's go.

85
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:24,199
Let's go.

86
00:04:24,759 --> 00:04:25,560
Come on.

87
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,759
Let's see how their members train.

88
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:30,519
Come on, this way.

89
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:31,720
Know your enemy, know yourself.

90
00:04:35,439 --> 00:04:36,800
They usually train right here.

91
00:04:37,519 --> 00:04:38,720
You two should come run around here when you're free.

92
00:04:43,319 --> 00:04:43,920
Keep it up!

93
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,439
This facility is of international standards.

94
00:04:45,439 --> 00:04:46,120
Keep it up!

95
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:46,560
Right.

96
00:04:47,199 --> 00:04:47,720
It's all the same.

97
00:04:48,319 --> 00:04:49,759
Keep it up! Keep it up!

98
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,480
Three minutes and 21 seconds.

99
00:04:58,560 --> 00:04:59,800
Not bad. Three minutes and 21 seconds.

100
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,439
Brother Lang.

101
00:05:04,199 --> 00:05:05,120
Well, if it isn't Xie.

102
00:05:06,199 --> 00:05:07,040
How long has it been?

103
00:05:08,319 --> 00:05:09,160
It's been a while, right?

104
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,959
Was it the boxing match last year or the year before?

105
00:05:10,959 --> 00:05:11,279
Right?

106
00:05:11,839 --> 00:05:13,000
Yeah, I lost to you.

107
00:05:14,319 --> 00:05:15,040
You went easy on me.

108
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,160
Otherwise I wouldn't have won.

109
00:05:16,199 --> 00:05:17,040
I'm older than you.

110
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,160
I really didn't expect

111
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,319
we'd get a chance to meet again.

112
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:19,959
Why is that?

113
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,000
Didn't they say you transferred to the Traffic Police?

114
00:05:22,439 --> 00:05:24,759
Not a transfer. I was loaned to the Traffic Police.

115
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:25,639
Now I'm back.

116
00:05:25,839 --> 00:05:26,360
You're back.

117
00:05:26,879 --> 00:05:27,439
Looking to retire?

118
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,160
The Special Police Unit isn't the right place for that.

119
00:05:29,759 --> 00:05:31,040
I don't like the sound of that.

120
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:32,439
What was your time just now?

121
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,160
Three minutes and 21 seconds.

122
00:05:33,759 --> 00:05:35,319
Three minutes and 21 seconds.

123
00:05:35,959 --> 00:05:36,600
Just okay, I guess.

124
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:37,639
Just okay?

125
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,920
Our unit definitely can't compare to the Traffic Police.

126
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:40,560
Must be "just okay".

127
00:05:40,639 --> 00:05:42,240
Right? How about we spar a bit?

128
00:05:43,199 --> 00:05:43,639
After you.

129
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:44,360
Alright.

130
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,240
Then I'll give it a shot, Comrades.

131
00:05:46,839 --> 00:05:47,720
Yeah!

132
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:50,839
They're sparring!

133
00:05:50,839 --> 00:05:51,399
They really are!

134
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,120
They are!

135
00:05:59,079 --> 00:06:00,079
Come on, Coach!

136
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:28,399
Your Captain Liu is in pretty good shape.

137
00:06:28,399 --> 00:06:30,040
Yeah, he trains regularly too.

138
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,000
Come on! Go, Coach!

139
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,600
Okay.

140
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,160
Three twenty-eight.

141
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:05,279
Good.

142
00:07:08,639 --> 00:07:10,240
Still a bit behind Captain Xie.

143
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,720
Just a little bit. Just a little bit.

144
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:16,560
The spirit of your Red Leaf Detachment

145
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,600
is worth learning from.

146
00:07:18,519 --> 00:07:20,120
Do you want to take a rest?

147
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:22,879
No need. Just train as usual.

148
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,519
We are here to learn.

149
00:07:26,199 --> 00:07:26,920
You've got youth on your side.

150
00:07:27,279 --> 00:07:28,040
Keep up the good work.

151
00:07:30,879 --> 00:07:31,879
I can't. I can't. I can't.

152
00:07:31,879 --> 00:07:32,399
Dismissed, everyone.

153
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,120
Xiao Xie is still the best.

154
00:07:35,759 --> 00:07:36,399
Is your back okay, Coach?

155
00:07:36,519 --> 00:07:37,360
I'm fine. I'm fine. I'm fine.

156
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:00,680
What are you doing, son?

157
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,720
I'm doing my homework right now.

158
00:08:04,879 --> 00:08:05,879
Still doing homework?

159
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,319
Go play for a while.

160
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:10,040
I haven't finished my homework yet.

161
00:08:11,279 --> 00:08:11,680
Listen...

162
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,480
As long as you finish it by Sunday night, it's fine.

163
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,720
When you play, just focus on playing.

164
00:08:15,879 --> 00:08:16,759
Play to your heart's content.

165
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:18,160
And when you do your homework,

166
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,800
you focus and take it seriously.

167
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,480
Don't mix the two.

168
00:08:22,079 --> 00:08:22,519
Understand?

169
00:08:22,959 --> 00:08:23,639
Really, Dad?

170
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,439
Did something good happen again?

171
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:26,920
Nothing special.

172
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:28,519
Tell your mom

173
00:08:29,199 --> 00:08:30,360
not to cook dinner for you tonight.

174
00:08:30,879 --> 00:08:32,200
I'm taking you out for steak.

175
00:08:33,639 --> 00:08:34,440
Dad will be home soon.

176
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:35,480
Okay.

177
00:08:38,679 --> 00:08:40,080
That's how kids should be raised.

178
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:42,720
No high-pressure parenting.

179
00:08:44,159 --> 00:08:45,799
Captain Liu, do you and Commander Xie

180
00:08:46,279 --> 00:08:46,879
know each other?

181
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:48,960
Of course I know him.

182
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:50,279
We're old friends.

183
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,480
And longtime rivals, too.

184
00:08:52,679 --> 00:08:53,960
He's never beaten me.

185
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,159
Then why didn't you just

186
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:58,960
let him win for once today?

187
00:08:58,960 --> 00:08:59,879
What would be the harm?

188
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:02,200
Especially when you're at your old friend's unit.

189
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,200
Anything goes in private.

190
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:05,879
But I won't hold back on the field.

191
00:09:08,639 --> 00:09:09,279
Captain Liu.

192
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,000
That move of yours today

193
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,480
gave me quite a scare.

194
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,440
That was just an accident, Commissar Tan.

195
00:09:16,679 --> 00:09:17,600
I know.

196
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,759
I spent too much time in the Traffic Police.

197
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:22,200
I'm out of practice.

198
00:09:22,639 --> 00:09:24,080
I'll make up for it when I get back.

199
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,399
I'll add an extra five kilometers every day,

200
00:09:26,919 --> 00:09:27,720
and 500 push-ups.

201
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:28,679
Don't worry.

202
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:29,720
I definitely won't drop the ball.

203
00:09:33,799 --> 00:09:34,759
Showing off.

204
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,399
I'm heading back to be with my son.

205
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,960
Is Ms. Chen here?

206
00:10:56,879 --> 00:10:57,559
Ms. Chen.

207
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:04,120
Ms. Chen.

208
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:08,840
Commissar Tan.

209
00:11:09,799 --> 00:11:10,320
Ms. Chen.

210
00:11:10,519 --> 00:11:11,200
Commissar Tan.

211
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:12,440
I'd like to

212
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,759
take up some of your time to chat.

213
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,799
You're here about Director Ji, right?

214
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,159
I'm not asking about her.

215
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:20,840
I have a question.

216
00:11:21,039 --> 00:11:21,799
I want to talk to you.

217
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:25,200
Have you heard of the 2-18 Hostage Case?

218
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,120
Of course I have.

219
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:29,039
The entire Red Leaf police system

220
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,200
knows about you two

221
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:32,519
and your heroic standoff with the suspect.

222
00:11:33,679 --> 00:11:35,519
But my wife, Ji Min, doesn't think so.

223
00:11:36,639 --> 00:11:37,799
I think she's blaming me.

224
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:42,320
The night after the 2-18 case ended,

225
00:11:43,159 --> 00:11:45,879
she sent me her message to Comrade Lu Zhong:

226
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
"Love others as yourself,

227
00:11:48,759 --> 00:11:49,639
be dedicated and responsible."

228
00:11:52,639 --> 00:11:53,919
Is it possible

229
00:11:54,559 --> 00:11:55,759
she also wanted to remind you

230
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:58,519
to have a little more empathy for others in life?

231
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:00,799
Ms. Chen,

232
00:12:01,639 --> 00:12:03,720
I started in political work.

233
00:12:04,399 --> 00:12:06,559
Empathy is the most basic skill.

234
00:12:10,039 --> 00:12:10,960
Then, Commissar Tan,

235
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:14,000
when you and Director Ji have conflicts in life,

236
00:12:14,639 --> 00:12:15,960
how do you resolve them?

237
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:17,799
My approach is,

238
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,200
first,

239
00:12:19,279 --> 00:12:21,720
clarify exactly whose responsibility it is.

240
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:24,320
Second, find the main issues of the conflict

241
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,240
and tackle them one by one.

242
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,919
Then set phased goals,

243
00:12:27,519 --> 00:12:28,240
advancing step by step.

244
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,279
Is there a problem?

245
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,320
What's your opinion, Ms. Chen?

246
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,519
I noticed that you and Director Ji

247
00:12:39,519 --> 00:12:41,600
share a similar mindset.

248
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:42,919
When encountering a problem,

249
00:12:43,279 --> 00:12:44,720
you instinctively switch back

250
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:45,879
to your familiar modes.

251
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:48,440
Just like now,

252
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:51,000
you switched back to Commissar mode.

253
00:12:52,799 --> 00:12:53,799
What mode is Ji Min in?

254
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,360
When Director Ji sits here,

255
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:58,120
she unconsciously straightens her back.

256
00:12:58,639 --> 00:13:00,399
This must be her posture at work.

257
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,720
She has already carried her work mode

258
00:13:02,799 --> 00:13:04,039
over into her life.

259
00:13:07,279 --> 00:13:08,159
But Commissar Tan,

260
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:10,480
in married life,

261
00:13:11,039 --> 00:13:12,159
there is no Director,

262
00:13:12,919 --> 00:13:14,039
and no Commissar.

263
00:13:14,159 --> 00:13:14,799
Do you agree?

264
00:13:15,639 --> 00:13:16,960
I agree.

265
00:13:17,279 --> 00:13:18,200
I totally agree.

266
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:19,360
That's exactly what I do.

267
00:13:19,759 --> 00:13:21,000
I buy vegetables and meat every day,

268
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:22,639
proof and knead the dough,

269
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,000
and steam buns and rolls.

270
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
I even prepare her foot bath.

271
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,440
This is the "good husband" mode.

272
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:30,320
Ji Min is indeed in Director mode.

273
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,480
Carrying this work mode

274
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,639
over into life

275
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:34,879
is unhealthy.

276
00:13:35,559 --> 00:13:38,559
Demanding perfection in life.

277
00:13:39,159 --> 00:13:40,000
At work,

278
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:41,600
taking on others' business

279
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,360
and others' responsibilities

280
00:13:44,759 --> 00:13:46,080
all onto her own shoulders.

281
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,000
Loving others more than herself.

282
00:13:48,879 --> 00:13:50,639
A classic obsessive-compulsive personality.

283
00:13:54,799 --> 00:13:56,120
Let's talk about your problems.

284
00:13:56,639 --> 00:13:57,480
I don't have any problems.

285
00:13:57,480 --> 00:13:59,559
I came here to figure out her problems.

286
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:06,279
Ms. Chen,

287
00:14:06,279 --> 00:14:08,360
do you have any other

288
00:14:08,519 --> 00:14:09,679
psychological methods?

289
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,240
The separation of tasks.

290
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,320
Whoever's problem it is, solves it.

291
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,200
You're back.

292
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,279
I ordered contact lenses.

293
00:14:54,519 --> 00:14:55,480
They were mailed to the house.

294
00:14:56,759 --> 00:14:57,720
For the Special Police Unit,

295
00:14:58,279 --> 00:14:59,879
we have to wear gear on missions.

296
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:02,159
Wearing framed glasses is inconvenient.

297
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:06,480
Where's the bed?

298
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:10,360
Familiar environment, right?

299
00:15:11,159 --> 00:15:12,320
It's all about relaxing.

300
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,279
What time do you go to work tomorrow?

301
00:15:44,679 --> 00:15:45,559
Tomorrow is the weekend.

302
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:48,000
You have the day off tomorrow.

303
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:48,960
I requested time off too.

304
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:50,679
Let's talk.

305
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:56,120
I've been thinking a lot lately.

306
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:58,120
About the message you wrote to Lu Zhong.

307
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:00,720
It was beautifully written.

308
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,279
Love others as yourself, be dedicated and responsible.

309
00:16:09,679 --> 00:16:10,840
That's exactly how you are.

310
00:16:15,399 --> 00:16:16,919
You remember when we were sophomores, right?

311
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:20,399
There was a singing competition at school.

312
00:16:21,519 --> 00:16:22,519
If it weren't for you,

313
00:16:22,559 --> 00:16:24,679
I wouldn't have had the courage to stand on that stage.

314
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,360
You are my Little Sunshine.

315
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,399
These past few days, I...

316
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,080
I've been reflecting on myself.

317
00:16:36,279 --> 00:16:37,279
I haven't cared enough about you.

318
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:39,879
In many ways,

319
00:16:39,879 --> 00:16:42,639
I still neglected your feelings.

320
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:47,600
I really have.

321
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,519
Just watch my actions from now on.

322
00:16:56,679 --> 00:16:57,279
Okay?

323
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,559
If there's ever an issue...

324
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:01,720
let's be more understanding,

325
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:02,519
and communicate more.

326
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:04,119
I'll be more understanding of you.

327
00:17:07,319 --> 00:17:08,200
If you have

328
00:17:08,799 --> 00:17:09,680
any complaints about me,

329
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,200
or if anything upsets you at work,

330
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:15,359
you can always tell me.

331
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:16,720
Just tell me.

332
00:17:17,079 --> 00:17:18,279
If you... if you ask more of me,

333
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,640
that's the only way I can improve.

334
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:26,799
Little Sunshine.

335
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:30,279
Can you give me another chance to improve?

336
00:17:53,759 --> 00:17:55,599
We don't need to go to Ms. Chen's anymore.

337
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:56,960
No need to go.

338
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,519
We will take it step by step together.

339
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,319
Little by little.

340
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:06,440
Slowly heal and adjust.

341
00:18:07,279 --> 00:18:10,599
Defeat this obsessive-compulsive personality together.

342
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:15,200
I... I firmly believe, I firmly believe, I firmly believe.

343
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,400
My obsessive-compulsive personality.

344
00:18:21,599 --> 00:18:22,559
I can understand.

345
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:24,200
Working at the police station,

346
00:18:24,319 --> 00:18:25,440
you're so busy.

347
00:18:25,559 --> 00:18:26,599
You have a strong sense of responsibility.

348
00:18:26,599 --> 00:18:28,559
You carry everything on your own shoulders.

349
00:18:28,559 --> 00:18:30,599
And always empathize with others' situations.

350
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,599
It really breaks my heart.

351
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:32,359
You work so hard.

352
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:34,039
I specifically went to consult Ms. Chen.

353
00:18:34,039 --> 00:18:35,079
About your situation,

354
00:18:35,079 --> 00:18:36,119
and how to deal with it.

355
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:37,319
How to deal with it?

356
00:18:38,839 --> 00:18:40,000
How to deal with it?

357
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:42,359
Separation of tasks.

358
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:43,319
Whoever's responsibility it is,

359
00:18:43,319 --> 00:18:43,960
that's who... who... who...

360
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:44,759
should be responsible.

361
00:18:44,759 --> 00:18:45,559
Just like you.

362
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:52,200
I...

363
00:18:53,839 --> 00:18:54,920
I'm just saying... saying...

364
00:18:55,119 --> 00:18:55,920
Did I say something wrong?

365
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:08,799
It's getting late.

366
00:19:08,799 --> 00:19:10,640
Go back and get some rest.

367
00:19:53,079 --> 00:19:55,160
Coach, run! The last 100 meters!

368
00:19:55,279 --> 00:19:56,079
You're there!

369
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:58,160
Keep going! Keep going! Keep going!

370
00:19:58,200 --> 00:19:58,799
Keep running!

371
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:08,000
I can't. My back is giving out.

372
00:20:10,079 --> 00:20:10,799
That's enough, Coach.

373
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,880
Don't be so hard on yourself.

374
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,759
What the hell do you know?

375
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:24,079
As a veteran Comrade,

376
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,400
three minutes and 28 seconds on the obstacle course...

377
00:20:28,119 --> 00:20:28,839
I'm not satisfied.

378
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:31,400
I should be

379
00:20:31,759 --> 00:20:32,880
setting an excellent example

380
00:20:33,519 --> 00:20:34,839
for all our Comrades.

381
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:36,920
But seriously, Coach,

382
00:20:37,359 --> 00:20:39,880
your lumbar strain is getting worse.

383
00:20:40,359 --> 00:20:41,880
You really need to be careful with your training.

384
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:43,680
Just that incident yesterday...

385
00:20:44,079 --> 00:20:45,440
It still scares me to think about it.

386
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:47,359
If something happened to you,

387
00:20:47,359 --> 00:20:48,359
how would I explain it to your wife?

388
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:49,480
Why explain anything to her?

389
00:20:50,599 --> 00:20:51,640
What's there to explain?

390
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,880
Ever since she married me,

391
00:20:55,759 --> 00:20:57,279
she should have been mentally prepared.

392
00:20:58,759 --> 00:21:00,200
Come on, Coach. There are no outsiders here.

393
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:02,480
Why are you acting so tough with me?

394
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:03,400
Who's acting tough?

395
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,079
When have I ever been soft?

396
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:06,640
You don't believe me?

397
00:21:09,599 --> 00:21:10,400
Lend me some money.

398
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:13,119
How much?

399
00:21:14,279 --> 00:21:14,920
1,680.

400
00:21:16,559 --> 00:21:17,799
Why such a specific amount?

401
00:21:21,359 --> 00:21:22,319
Making up for your bonus, huh?

402
00:21:22,839 --> 00:21:23,680
I'll transfer it to you now.

403
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:25,640
Don't transfer it. I want cash.

404
00:21:26,359 --> 00:21:27,119
Put it in a red envelope for me.

405
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:28,839
I get it.

406
00:21:29,799 --> 00:21:30,880
Go back and tell your wife

407
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:32,960
that the bonus is in cash this time.

408
00:21:35,039 --> 00:21:36,079
You think you know it all.

409
00:21:36,839 --> 00:21:38,160
Showing off, aren't you?

410
00:21:39,799 --> 00:21:40,440
Captain Liu,

411
00:21:43,279 --> 00:21:44,160
hurry up!

412
00:21:44,279 --> 00:21:45,400
How are you slower than me?

413
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:46,720
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

414
00:21:46,839 --> 00:21:47,279
Captain Liu!

415
00:21:48,519 --> 00:21:49,000
What's wrong?

416
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,359
Ma'am brought Da Zhuang to the unit!

417
00:21:53,759 --> 00:21:54,279
What?

418
00:21:59,000 --> 00:21:59,680
Commander Liao,

419
00:22:00,279 --> 00:22:01,279
tell me the truth.

420
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:02,960
Is Liu Lang having an affair?

421
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:05,519
That's impossible, Ma'am.

422
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,599
Brother Lang is definitely not that kind of guy.

423
00:22:08,359 --> 00:22:10,440
With people, anything is possible.

424
00:22:11,359 --> 00:22:12,920
He never used to lie.

425
00:22:13,559 --> 00:22:16,119
Now he lies effortlessly.

426
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,599
Yesterday he was at the Traffic Police,

427
00:22:19,079 --> 00:22:20,359
out checking for drunk drivers.

428
00:22:21,039 --> 00:22:22,079
Today he got paid,

429
00:22:22,359 --> 00:22:25,200
and the payer was the Special Police Unit.

430
00:22:29,319 --> 00:22:30,119
These days,

431
00:22:30,799 --> 00:22:32,559
he's either working overtime or covering shifts.

432
00:22:33,119 --> 00:22:34,200
Or else he tells me

433
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:36,079
he has to stay in the dorm for duty.

434
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:37,640
Tell me,

435
00:22:38,559 --> 00:22:39,559
does that sound like an affair?

436
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:40,359
Well, uh,

437
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,799
Brother Lang is definitely not that kind of guy.

438
00:22:41,799 --> 00:22:43,039
I can guarantee that, Ma'am.

439
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:44,079
Really.

440
00:22:44,599 --> 00:22:45,559
Right now,

441
00:22:45,759 --> 00:22:46,799
he's at the unit every day,

442
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:48,119
training Lü Xiao and the others.

443
00:22:48,559 --> 00:22:49,359
But as for him

444
00:22:49,759 --> 00:22:51,440
returning to the Special Police Unit behind your back,

445
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:52,279
I honestly didn't know.

446
00:22:53,119 --> 00:22:55,799
Before, I had him seconded to the Traffic Police

447
00:22:56,519 --> 00:22:57,920
just for some stability.

448
00:22:58,640 --> 00:23:00,279
For his own good, and for our family's good.

449
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:02,319
Was I wrong?

450
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:04,000
No, you weren't, Ma'am.

451
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:09,240
Let's not even mention the benefits.

452
00:23:10,039 --> 00:23:11,920
Going on missions during holidays is normal.

453
00:23:12,119 --> 00:23:13,599
You even have to be on the front lines.

454
00:23:14,279 --> 00:23:16,880
Have I ever held you guys back all these years?

455
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:17,359
No.

456
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,960
Haven't I fully supported you?

457
00:23:22,799 --> 00:23:23,400
Commander Liao,

458
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:25,400
how about this.

459
00:23:25,799 --> 00:23:27,319
Go call Captain Liu back immediately.

460
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:31,039
Right, right.

461
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:36,960
Take Da Zhuang outside for a walk, too.

462
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:38,079
Right. Zhuang, let's go.

463
00:23:43,079 --> 00:23:43,799
Hello, Ma'am.

464
00:23:44,039 --> 00:23:45,480
I'm the new Commissar.

465
00:23:46,079 --> 00:23:47,359
My last name is Tan. Tan Yan.

466
00:23:48,039 --> 00:23:49,039
This is our first time meeting.

467
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:50,400
Commissar Tan.

468
00:23:52,359 --> 00:23:54,279
Based on what you've just told me,

469
00:23:54,559 --> 00:23:55,599
I basically understand the situation.

470
00:23:59,039 --> 00:24:00,240
That one in the front is me.

471
00:24:02,359 --> 00:24:04,519
That was when we trained together.

472
00:24:08,759 --> 00:24:09,400
This is your dad.

473
00:24:13,039 --> 00:24:15,519
That was back in 2017.

474
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:19,119
Your dad caught three home invaders by himself.

475
00:24:26,279 --> 00:24:28,039
Didn't your dad tell you about this?

476
00:24:30,359 --> 00:24:31,440
He mentioned it before.

477
00:24:32,559 --> 00:24:34,160
But later, afraid my mom would worry,

478
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:36,160
he stopped talking about it.

479
00:24:38,119 --> 00:24:38,920
My mom says

480
00:24:39,599 --> 00:24:41,000
my dad is a good cop,

481
00:24:41,839 --> 00:24:43,079
but not a good dad.

482
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:51,480
Then what makes a good dad?

483
00:24:53,079 --> 00:24:54,640
One who spends plenty of quality time.

484
00:24:56,359 --> 00:24:58,039
And what counts as quality time?

485
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:01,680
Just spending more time with your child.

486
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:05,039
Going to the amusement park, the zoo...

487
00:25:05,519 --> 00:25:07,240
Joining in family activities...

488
00:25:07,759 --> 00:25:08,920
Stuff like that, I guess.

489
00:25:09,559 --> 00:25:10,720
It's actually pretty boring.

490
00:25:13,240 --> 00:25:15,480
Did your dad take you to these places?

491
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:18,880
All of them.

492
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:20,960
My dad is actually alright.

493
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:23,279
When he's home, he always spends time with me.

494
00:25:24,839 --> 00:25:26,119
It's just that he's rarely home.

495
00:25:37,279 --> 00:25:37,880
Commissar Tan.

496
00:25:38,519 --> 00:25:40,200
You're absolutely right about that.

497
00:25:41,599 --> 00:25:42,839
It's not easy being a police officer.

498
00:25:42,839 --> 00:25:44,039
Everyone can see that.

499
00:25:44,839 --> 00:25:46,599
But what about us police spouses?

500
00:25:47,359 --> 00:25:48,839
The hardships we go through...

501
00:25:48,839 --> 00:25:50,519
how many people actually see that?

502
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:52,960
When I was giving birth to Da Zhuang,

503
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:54,680
Old Liu took me to the hospital.

504
00:25:54,839 --> 00:25:56,079
Before I even got to the delivery room,

505
00:25:56,079 --> 00:25:57,400
he got a call from the team.

506
00:25:57,920 --> 00:25:59,000
He left me all alone

507
00:25:59,480 --> 00:26:00,519
and went on a mission.

508
00:26:01,519 --> 00:26:02,880
I was alone in the delivery room,

509
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:04,359
in absolute agony.

510
00:26:05,119 --> 00:26:06,720
At that time, I thought to myself,

511
00:26:07,319 --> 00:26:08,200
when he gets back,

512
00:26:08,680 --> 00:26:09,519
I'm definitely going to

513
00:26:09,519 --> 00:26:10,759
slap him hard in the face.

514
00:26:16,039 --> 00:26:17,119
But when he

515
00:26:17,880 --> 00:26:18,759
finally came back,

516
00:26:21,160 --> 00:26:23,640
and I saw the injuries on him...

517
00:26:26,279 --> 00:26:28,799
He had rushed back without even wiping the blood off.

518
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:34,920
I just couldn't bring myself

519
00:26:37,039 --> 00:26:39,079
to actually slap him.

520
00:26:53,359 --> 00:26:54,000
Commissar Tan.

521
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:56,039
I came here today

522
00:26:56,559 --> 00:26:57,440
with only one demand.

523
00:26:58,839 --> 00:26:59,440
Old Liu

524
00:27:00,079 --> 00:27:00,839
must be transferred.

525
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:08,839
Captain Liu is back.

526
00:27:10,359 --> 00:27:11,640
He just finished a five-kilometer run.

527
00:27:17,599 --> 00:27:18,240
Commissar Tan,

528
00:27:19,519 --> 00:27:20,839
my stance is firm.

529
00:27:22,519 --> 00:27:23,680
The Special Police Unit needs me.

530
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:25,599
Liu Lang!

531
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,599
Have you forgotten what you promised me?

532
00:27:28,359 --> 00:27:29,400
Honey, please calm down.

533
00:27:30,559 --> 00:27:32,119
Let's talk about this at home, okay?

534
00:27:32,119 --> 00:27:33,079
There's nothing to hide.

535
00:27:33,079 --> 00:27:34,119
Why do we have to talk at home?

536
00:27:34,839 --> 00:27:36,440
I'm putting my foot down today.

537
00:27:36,559 --> 00:27:37,480
Commissar Tan is here, too.

538
00:27:38,799 --> 00:27:40,279
If you still want this family,

539
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:42,640
you'll write that transfer application today.

540
00:27:45,519 --> 00:27:47,160
Honey, listen to me.

541
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:49,480
Transferring is a big deal.

542
00:27:50,519 --> 00:27:51,839
It's not as simple as you think.

543
00:27:52,559 --> 00:27:53,359
By causing a scene here,

544
00:27:53,839 --> 00:27:57,640
we're... we're just making trouble for Commissar Tan.

545
00:27:57,640 --> 00:27:59,279
You know? It puts him in a tough spot.

546
00:28:00,079 --> 00:28:01,200
I... No...

547
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:02,839
I'm... I'm not in a tough spot.

548
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:05,839
Captain Liu, this is a big deal.

549
00:28:07,119 --> 00:28:08,039
I'm giving you a week off.

550
00:28:08,519 --> 00:28:10,160
Go home and talk it over with Ma'am.

551
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:11,000
No, no, no.

552
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:12,279
There's really no need.

553
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:13,240
Talk it over.

554
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:17,079
I disagree.

555
00:28:21,480 --> 00:28:22,880
You... You see this?

556
00:28:22,960 --> 00:28:24,240
That's his attitude.

557
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:26,119
Tell me, how am I supposed to live like this?

558
00:28:26,839 --> 00:28:28,319
Life must go on, Ma'am.

559
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:29,680
Da Zhuang!

560
00:28:32,720 --> 00:28:33,440
Da Zhuang!

561
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,359
Get down here!

562
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:38,720
Coach.

563
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,599
Then why don't you just live here!

564
00:28:59,720 --> 00:29:00,640
What did Ma'am say?

565
00:29:03,599 --> 00:29:04,319
If I don't transfer,

566
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,160
we split up.

567
00:29:16,599 --> 00:29:17,559
What do you think

568
00:29:18,559 --> 00:29:20,240
about what happened at Headquarters?

569
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:22,920
Didn't Brother Lang already explain?

570
00:29:22,920 --> 00:29:24,559
He got rusty at the Traffic Police and slipped up.

571
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:27,039
Do you believe that?

572
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:34,160
I do.

573
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:53,359
No.

574
00:29:53,359 --> 00:29:55,759
You need a birth certificate for a kid's passport?

575
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,359
Isn't the household register enough?

576
00:30:01,400 --> 00:30:03,079
Okay, okay, thank you.

577
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,799
Hello, welcome.

578
00:30:13,039 --> 00:30:13,640
Coming!

579
00:30:15,319 --> 00:30:16,880
Hello, what can I get for you?

580
00:30:18,039 --> 00:30:20,400
These buns look good. What's the filling?

581
00:30:21,519 --> 00:30:23,240
Sorry, these are reserved for someone else.

582
00:30:23,240 --> 00:30:25,079
Take a look at what else we have in the store.

583
00:30:25,640 --> 00:30:26,240
Take your pick.

584
00:30:29,799 --> 00:30:31,000
I'll take some "Spring Snow".

585
00:30:49,720 --> 00:30:51,960
I've really never heard of that.

586
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:54,359
Maybe you should try another shop.

587
00:30:56,640 --> 00:30:57,880
If you don't have it here,

588
00:30:58,720 --> 00:31:01,400
nowhere else will either.

589
00:31:03,519 --> 00:31:04,559
What's this?

590
00:31:07,279 --> 00:31:07,880
Naonao.

591
00:31:08,960 --> 00:31:10,200
Go play in your room. Hurry up.

592
00:31:20,799 --> 00:31:22,279
This is a pretty good spot.

593
00:31:23,400 --> 00:31:24,200
Right outside the Special Police Unit.

594
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:26,079
Yeah.

595
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:28,799
Their security cameras cover this exact area.

596
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:31,119
That's good.

597
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:32,440
It's safe.

598
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:37,720
But can you live here for the rest of your life?

599
00:31:47,759 --> 00:31:48,559
Relax.

600
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:51,319
We're here to help you.

601
00:31:55,720 --> 00:31:56,759
Who are you?

602
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:00,319
Remember Gangzi?

603
00:32:02,359 --> 00:32:02,920
I don't know him.

604
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:06,960
The guy the cops shot dead.

605
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:08,680
Jin Yonggang.

606
00:32:16,039 --> 00:32:17,759
Come with me. Someone wants to see you.

607
00:32:21,759 --> 00:32:22,680
Did Lu Haifeng send you?

608
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:24,599
Doesn't matter who. Just come with me.

609
00:32:24,720 --> 00:32:25,079
Move.

610
00:32:25,559 --> 00:32:26,119
What are you doing?

611
00:32:26,440 --> 00:32:27,039
Help!

612
00:32:27,039 --> 00:32:28,680
Keep yelling and I'll kill you!

613
00:32:29,799 --> 00:32:30,839
Don't scare the kid.

614
00:32:31,559 --> 00:32:32,440
I'll give you money.

615
00:32:34,920 --> 00:32:36,480
You're the ones who told him to find me?

616
00:32:42,759 --> 00:32:44,279
The cop in the Mahjong Parlor,

617
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:46,759
you killed him too?

618
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:48,559
Yeah.

619
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,440
What do you want?

620
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:02,039
Let's work together.

621
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:06,559
You can name your terms.

622
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:08,960
Whatever Lu Haifeng can offer,

623
00:33:09,559 --> 00:33:10,400
we can offer.

624
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:13,839
Whatever Lu Haifeng can't offer,

625
00:33:15,559 --> 00:33:16,599
we can offer too.

626
00:33:22,079 --> 00:33:23,839
Whether I can leave isn't up to me.

627
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:26,680
Lu Haifeng's men are right over there.

628
00:33:28,559 --> 00:33:29,279
Why don't

629
00:33:31,279 --> 00:33:33,039
you go talk it over with them first?

630
00:34:02,400 --> 00:34:02,839
Brother Yong

631
00:34:39,519 --> 00:34:41,960
Call your Boss Lu.

632
00:34:43,239 --> 00:34:44,039
I want to see him.

633
00:34:51,679 --> 00:34:52,760
Mention Mr. Bai to him.

634
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:12,400
Okay.

635
00:35:13,559 --> 00:35:14,719
I'll bring them over right away.

636
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:29,079
Mr. Lu, they're here.

637
00:35:44,679 --> 00:35:45,199
Do you play?

638
00:35:47,119 --> 00:35:47,519
A little.

639
00:35:50,159 --> 00:35:50,559
Let's play a round.

640
00:35:57,960 --> 00:35:58,880
Let them talk first.

641
00:35:59,559 --> 00:35:59,920
Alright.

642
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:01,199
Let's go.

643
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:38,199
Mr. Bai and I go way back.

644
00:36:39,119 --> 00:36:40,679
Doing business together all these years

645
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:42,800
has been quite pleasant.

646
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:44,960
I welcome you as my guests.

647
00:36:45,760 --> 00:36:48,559
But only if you play by the rules.

648
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:51,159
What doesn't belong to you,

649
00:36:52,079 --> 00:36:52,920
keep your hands off.

650
00:36:54,039 --> 00:36:54,559
Mr. Lu.

651
00:36:55,639 --> 00:36:57,239
Everyone wants a piece of a good thing.

652
00:36:58,239 --> 00:36:59,519
If you can't protect it yourself,

653
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:01,239
and won't let others step in,

654
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:03,159
that's hardly fair.

655
00:37:05,760 --> 00:37:07,320
Nobody takes what's mine.

656
00:37:08,440 --> 00:37:10,199
Pack up and head back tomorrow.

657
00:37:11,159 --> 00:37:12,119
As for what happened today,

658
00:37:13,039 --> 00:37:13,960
I'll let it slide.

659
00:37:14,760 --> 00:37:15,639
When you get back,

660
00:37:16,559 --> 00:37:18,000
give my regards to Mr. Bai.

661
00:37:18,119 --> 00:37:19,880
I can't pass those on for you.

662
00:37:21,119 --> 00:37:22,360
Mr. Bai is gone.

663
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:24,400
I did it.

664
00:37:36,039 --> 00:37:37,199
For future cooperation,

665
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:39,239
you talk to me.

666
00:37:52,159 --> 00:37:52,960
You've set up your own operation.

667
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:57,840
Congratulations.

668
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:03,719
As long as it doesn't hurt my bottom line,

669
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:08,519
I don't care who I work with.

670
00:38:08,519 --> 00:38:09,079
It's not the same.

671
00:38:11,199 --> 00:38:13,000
From now on, I supply the goods.

672
00:38:14,159 --> 00:38:15,199
And you handle distribution.

673
00:38:26,039 --> 00:38:27,599
That depends on if you have what it takes.

674
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:00,039
Kitty.

675
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:01,679
Kitty.

676
00:39:03,360 --> 00:39:04,079
Kitty.

677
00:39:05,480 --> 00:39:06,599
Looks like my brother

678
00:39:07,239 --> 00:39:08,760
went easy today.

679
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:12,800
Otherwise, your boys wouldn't have survived.

680
00:39:20,840 --> 00:39:22,039
Leave the woman alone.

681
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,199
I'm taking her away in a couple of days.

682
00:39:29,119 --> 00:39:30,039
And if I say no?

683
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:35,239
Then someone's going to lose their life.

684
00:39:37,599 --> 00:39:38,360
Either yours,

685
00:39:39,440 --> 00:39:40,320
or mine.

686
00:39:52,400 --> 00:39:53,599
What a cute cat!

687
00:39:55,480 --> 00:39:55,920
Let's go.

688
00:41:23,119 --> 00:41:24,159
This is family business.

689
00:41:25,079 --> 00:41:26,480
Why drag outsiders into it?

690
00:41:28,159 --> 00:41:29,280
You wouldn't let me leave.

691
00:41:30,639 --> 00:41:32,280
So I had to find my own way out.

692
00:41:34,800 --> 00:41:36,119
Are you really so sure

693
00:41:37,480 --> 00:41:39,280
they can get you out of Red Leaf?

694
00:41:42,199 --> 00:41:43,039
It seems

695
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:44,920
you didn't handle them.

696
00:41:45,760 --> 00:41:47,360
Those two are bad news.

697
00:41:48,599 --> 00:41:49,760
Do you know what they want from you?

698
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:52,519
Give them even a taste of what they want,

699
00:41:53,679 --> 00:41:55,039
and they will never let you go.

700
00:41:55,239 --> 00:41:56,079
I told you,

701
00:41:57,719 --> 00:41:59,760
I have to get Naonao out for treatment.

702
00:42:01,599 --> 00:42:04,599
For him, I'm willing to risk everything.

703
00:42:06,039 --> 00:42:07,559
Did you see the photos I sent you?

704
00:42:09,480 --> 00:42:10,400
What is this supposed to mean?

705
00:42:11,840 --> 00:42:13,239
Are these the companions you found for Naonao?

706
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:17,000
I spent a lot of time

707
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:18,320
tracking down these three kids.

708
00:42:19,119 --> 00:42:21,320
Their height and build are similar to Naonao's.

709
00:42:22,039 --> 00:42:25,400
Their heart size and tissue typing are a match too.

710
00:42:30,159 --> 00:42:31,159
Lu Haifeng!

711
00:42:35,159 --> 00:42:36,320
You will rot in hell for this.

712
00:42:38,440 --> 00:42:39,880
For you and Naonao,

713
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:41,519
I'm willing to do anything.

714
00:42:43,079 --> 00:42:43,760
Oh, and one more thing.

715
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:46,480
I don't care what kind of relationship

716
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:47,639
you have with that Special Police captain.

717
00:42:50,920 --> 00:42:51,719
Stay away from him.

718
00:43:12,280 --> 00:43:14,320
If you don't take care of Lu Haifeng once and for all,

719
00:43:14,719 --> 00:43:15,559
I won't leave.

720
00:43:15,840 --> 00:43:17,360
You have to handle this, Commander Liao.

721
00:43:17,719 --> 00:43:19,360
About Naonao's psychological issues,

722
00:43:19,360 --> 00:43:21,000
you should take him out to play more often.

723
00:43:21,519 --> 00:43:22,079
Don't think

724
00:43:22,079 --> 00:43:24,119
that having a Special Police captain for a boyfriend

725
00:43:24,119 --> 00:43:24,920
makes you safe.

726
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:28,280
He told all the boatmen in Red Leaf,

727
00:43:28,719 --> 00:43:29,039
saying,

728
00:43:29,480 --> 00:43:30,559
you guys can leave,

729
00:43:30,559 --> 00:43:31,800
but you can't bring an extra person.

730
00:43:31,880 --> 00:43:34,119
We'll teach Lu Haifeng to behave.
